## Layout

```
nrw.toml                  project config
skills/                   domain skills, read by Claude Code and Copilot
samples/<id>/
  sample.md               your notes: description, measurements, fits to do
  sample.yaml             machine register of measurements on disk
  data/steady/            REFL_*_combined_data_auto.txt, REFL_*_partial.txt
  data/tnr/<run>_<bin>/   r<run>_t<seconds>.txt slices + reduction JSON
  data/raw/               NeXus (gitignored)
  models/<name>.yaml      model spec — the source of truth
  models/<name>.py        generated fit script — derived, do not hand-edit
  assessments/<label>/    tNR metric output
  results/<fit_id>/       immutable fit records
  reports/                write-ups
docs/ground_truths.md     findings that must survive between sessions
```

## Getting started

```bash
nrw doctor                       # check the environment
nrw sample new Sample1           # create a sample
# copy reduced data into samples/Sample1/data/steady/ and data/tnr/
nrw sample scan Sample1          # register what is on disk
```

Then open this folder in VS Code and work with Claude Code. It reads
`skills/reflectometry/` automatically through the dispatcher agents.

## The one rule

Every result must stay traceable to what produced it. Do not hand-edit
generated scripts, do not overwrite results, and run `nrw check` before calling
anything final. `nrw whence <figure>` should always be able to answer "what made
this?".
